{
 "about": "Front ID0: the id glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-id.md §5) that src/i18n/id/id.test.ts enforces through the SC4 lint framework (src/i18n/lint/, profile id) on every Indonesian string. Seeded from the French glossary: the same English patterns and interface names, re-targeted to Indonesian from the English (French and Spanish only as meaning context) and the plan's §5.2–§5.3 terms (Indonesian Wikipedia, ITB/Bosscha and BRIN usage, KBBI spelling; no IAU OAE Indonesian glossary exists, so these are usage, not an official standard). A term applies when its English pattern matches the English source: the Indonesian must then match the `id` stem or pattern. Names are fixed interface names (an exact name applies only to a whole string; the name match ignores case). Forbidden here are the term forms this glossary rejects (kepunahan, klaster, geser merah, redshift outside glosses, berkas for a computer file, peramban, magnitudo tampak/absolut, tetapan Hubble, pulsa); the language-wide rules (the «Anda» register, KBBI spellings, Malay words, diacritics, di-/ke- spacing, reduplication, quotes and thousands, claims) live in the id profile of src/i18n/lint/profiles.ts. VIREO's own names follow the plan's decided forms (Save → Simpan, Record → Catat, Find → Temukan, Search → Cari, Show → Tampilkan, Display → Tampilan, Slew → Gerakkan, Init/Go → Siapkan/Mulai, Scan → Telusuri, Clear → Kosongkan, Delete → Hapus, Reset → Atur Ulang, Hot List → daftar objek, lab → praktikum, file → file, browser → browser). Rows for areas later fronts translate are reviewed by those fronts before use.",
